"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3167 as a "for" detector.

The component writes a strong "for" signal into the residual stream. It is silent on
almost every token, but fires on the word "for" (any capitalisation, with or without a
leading space), and on "for" written in a few other languages (German "für", Russian
"для", Swedish "för", Dutch "voor", Indonesian "untuk", Romanian "pentru", Polish "dla";
Spanish "para" weaker). The size depends on the word before "for": after words of need
or suitability ("necessary for", "essential for", "needed for", "basis for") it is about
1.5 to 2; after words of seeking, waiting or thanks ("look for", "waiting for",
"thank you for", "responsible for") it is weak, about 0.3; otherwise about 1. The
nouns "basis", "foundation", "framework", "underlying" fire at about 0.7, the
purpose-sense "to" after "necessary"/"needed" at about 0.3.

The prediction looks only at the current word and the word before it.
