"""Detect tokens carrying an 'il' spelling, especially a short trailing -il.

Bare il and short fragments ending in -il have a large negative response.
The response weakens for longer fragments, -ail/-oil/-eil, doubled l, and
common English words. Utility-library notation is particularly strong.
Short /il/-like spellings in several other scripts receive a smaller response.
For bare il, the preceding token ending distinguishes oil, eil and quil.
Other tokens predict zero. Residual lexical and contextual variation is omitted.
